desc:Burl [West Coast drum machine] (GFX)
//author: GardenFX
// by JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//tags: instrument drum machine percussion west coast wavefolder low pass gate vactrol fm step sequencer
/*
  BURL - complex analog-style wavefold percussion machine.
  Six voices built on West Coast lines: an oscillator core pushed through a wavefolder, then a vactrol
  low-pass gate instead of an envelope and a VCA. Nothing is sampled.

  VOICES
  1 KICK     sine core with an exponential pitch drop (SNAP, SWEEP = how fast), a mild fold for chest.
  2 SNARE    two-operator, high-ratio FM (RATIO: wooden .. metallic) with a breath of noise; the rim
             (note 37) plays it as a claves: an octave and a fifth up, no noise, shorter.
  3 TOM 1    tuned triangle cores (the head and its first membrane mode) with a feedback LOOP
  4 TOM 2    (self-FM): wooden at 0, metallic congas and rings turned up.
  5 METAL    six square cores at inharmonic ratios, ring-modulated in pairs and high-passed (SPREAD
             widens the ratios); closed and open (notes 42 / 44 closed, 46 / 51 open; closed chokes open).
  6 BURST    noise and a sine into a resonant filter that self-oscillates near the top of RESO, swept by
             SNAP and folded: zaps, bleeps, scrapes.

  EVERY VOICE
  TUNE       +/- 24 semitones.   SNAP  how far the pitch falls on the strike (exponential).
  FOLD       the wavefolder: peaks fold back inward - brighter, metallic.  The fourth knob is the voice's
             CHARACTER: SWEEP, RATIO, LOOP, LOOP, SPREAD, RESO.
  STRIKE     the excitation: a short, soft pluck (the gate half opens: darker, quieter) up to a hard strike
             that opens it fully and pings it.
  DECAY      the gate's release, 20 ms - 3 s. Vactrol-like: fast at the top, a slow, sluggish tail.
  FM         how far this voice is cross-modulated by the FM BUS (the sum of all the other voices).
  PAN, LEVEL.
  The gate opens level and brightness together: harder (accented) hits are louder AND brighter.

  UNCERTAINTY GENERATOR  a sample-and-hold random voltage per step and per voice. AMOUNT (subtle to
             radical), and what it moves: PITCH, FOLD, DECAY. LOCK holds the sixteen values, so the bar repeats.
  VOLTAGE STRIPS  FOLD and DECAY: touch strips that push every voice's fold and decay, live (centre = none).
  SEQUENCER  16 steps of 1/16, four patterns (A - D: while running a new one takes over at the next bar, its key flashing until then), SWING. Each lane has its own LENGTH (1 - 16, the box at
             its right end: a list) for polymeters. Click a step: off -> hit -> accent -> off
             (METAL: off -> closed -> open -> off); drag to paint; right-click clears. RUN plays it at the
             project tempo; SYNC (lit by default) plays it with REAPER's transport. It never starts on its own.
  MIDI       36 / 35 kick, 38 / 40 snare, 37 claves, 48 / 50 tom 1, 45 / 47 / 43 / 41 / 58 tom 2,
             42 / 44 closed, 46 / 51 / 53 / 59 open metal, 49 / 52 / 55 / 57 burst. Velocity = strike.
  DRIFT      vactrol + oscillator wander: each voice's pitch and fold wander slowly, and its gate gets a
             little quicker or more sluggish, as warm optocouplers do.
  OUTPUT     level into an anti-aliased clipper (always on).
  GUI        click a voice's name to hear it and show it in the FOLD SCOPE (its live folded wave and its
             gate's decay curve). Knobs: drag (Shift = fine), wheel, double-click / Ctrl-click = default.
*/

import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc

in_pin:none
out_pin:Left
out_pin:Right

slider1:0<0,1,1{Stop,Run}>-Run
slider2:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Sync (follow REAPER's transport)
slider3:0<0,3,1{A,B,C,D}>-Pattern
slider4:10<0,75,1>-Swing (%)
slider5:20<0,100,0.1>-Uncertainty (%)
slider6:0<-100,100,0.1>-Fold strip
slider7:0<-100,100,0.1>-Decay strip
slider8:25<0,100,0.1>-Drift (%)
slider9:0<-24,12,0.1>-Output (dB)
slider10:0<-24,24,0.1>-Kick Tune (st)
slider11:55<0,100,0.1>-Kick Snap
slider12:20<0,100,0.1>-Kick Fold
slider13:30<0,100,0.1>-Kick Character
slider14:70<0,100,0.1>-Kick Strike
slider15:55<0,100,0.1>-Kick Decay
